{"qid":"Q816814","names":["Kingdom of Gwynedd"],"title":"Kingdom of Gwynedd","endonym":{"native":"Gwynedd","lang":"cy"},"capsule":"Gwynedd was the dominant Welsh kingdom of the early Middle Ages, centred on the mountainous fastness of Snowdonia and the fertile isle of Anglesey, and tracing its ruling line back to Cunedda in the late fourth century. Its greatest medieval expansion came under Llywelyn ap Iorwerth (Llywelyn the Great, r. 1195–1240) and Llywelyn ap Gruffudd (Llywelyn the Last), who in 1267 extracted recognition as Prince of Wales from Henry III under the Treaty of Montgomery. English conquest followed swiftly after Llywelyn's death in battle at Cilmeri in December 1282; Edward I's Statute of Rhuddlan in 1284 extinguished Welsh political autonomy and imposed English administration over the north.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Core Gwynedd territory is well-attested through Welsh annals and English administrative records, though exact boundaries in the sixth and seventh centuries are poorly defined.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Britannica: Gwynedd, kingdom, Wales","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Gwynedd-kingdom-Wales"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Kingdom of Gwynedd","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Gwynedd"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Llywelyn ap Gruffudd","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Llywelyn_ap_Gruffudd"}],"britannica":null,"cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Kingdom of Gwynedd","rulers":[{"qid":null,"name":"Maelgwn Gwynedd","nativeName":"Maelgwn Gwynedd","roman":"","start":520,"end":547,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Rhun ap Maelgw